# Backport of pytorch/ao#4880 ("Fix MoE FP8 Triton autotune key", commit
# 9e5ea7fde7132df0c09b2acb12c2defad90aecb9) to torchao v0.17.0 (commit
# 02105d46c61dc80a8c9d39d5836e827ba3af8439), file torchao/prototype/moe_training/kernels/float8_rowwise.py.
# The triton.autotune key of _triton_fp8_rowwise_3d_transpose_cast_rhs_kernel names "num_elements", which
# is not a kernel argument. Triton 3.9 (PyTorch 26.11 base) rejects such keys when
# torchao.prototype.moe_training is imported, which the MXFP8 grouped GEMM needs. Remove this patch when
# TORCHAO_REF moves past v0.17.0; the Docker build accepts only the original or the already-patched source.
